            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical treatment of the Palmaz-Schatz stent trapped in the left coronary ostium].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 72-year-old male with failed delivery of the Palmaz-Schatz stent to the coronary dissection following percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) was admitted to our hospital. He was very sick and required an emergent surgical procedures. We successfully carried out the bypass grafting to the LAD and removed the stent through the aortotomy. Besides his respiratory care, postoperative course was uneventful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
